    ! ---- pf_random_exp_at / pf_random_exp_portable_at ----
    !
    ! The same grid of coordinates as the scalar table above, on purpose: an
    ! exponential draw is a transform of pf_random_at at the SAME coordinate, so any
    ! row where the two tables disagree about which uniform was read is a defect in
    ! exactly one of them. exp_u repeats that uniform so the suite can say which.
    !
    ! The two realisations are pinned DIFFERENTLY, and the difference is the whole
    ! point of there being two:
    !
    !   exp_portable_bits  EXACT. parquet_expkey's frozen transform, re-derived in
    !                      Python rather than translated, and asserted bit for bit.
    !   exp_ref_bits       -log(1-u) at 60 significant digits, correctly rounded.
    !                      pf_random_exp_at uses the INTRINSIC log, so it is only
    !                      bit-identical for a given libm and must be asserted to a
    !                      few ulp of this. Asserting it exactly would make the suite
    !                      fail on the next libm, which is not what it is testing.
    !
